  "post_stream": {
    "posts": [
      {
        "id": 19324,
        "name": "kazaasaky",
        "username": "kazaasaky",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/e68b1a/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-07-22T09:31:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p><a href=\"https://querki.net/u/darker/spirit-island-faq/#!.9v5kbjr\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://querki.net/u/darker/spirit-island-faq/#!.9v5kbjr</a></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>You're being told to Push 2 Dahan from a single land with a City to a single land without a City. If that's impossible, but you can Push 1 Dahan following those constraints, do so. Otherwise, do nothing on that board.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>If '1 dahan can move without city' is possible, why text didn`t contain 'up to'?</p>\n<p>i think it must ' must only 2 dahan move, If that's impossible impossible, this event can`t move 1 dahan.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I'm confused because a sentence without 'up to' has the effect of including 'up to'.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:58.535Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
