        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>If it said \"up to\", you could choose to move only one Dahan even if there were more present, and that isn't the intent of the card. You need to fulfill as much as is possible, so if only one Dahan is present then only one Dahan can move. It's like in Sentinels if you're told to discard two cards but only have one in your hand, you would still discard that one.</p>",
